From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:04:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpio: apple,d2365-pmic-gpio: Add the D2355 and
 D2400

The A10X boards carry the August D2400 PMU, whose GPIO input levels read
as on the D2365 and whose 256 PMU events include the GPIO lines from event
0x30, and the D2355 charger PMU, of which only the 80-event block is
described, as for the D2089.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/interrupt-controller/0001 reworked: the event
 blocks are the existing PMIC GPIO node's ("apple,d2355-pmic-gpio",
 "apple,d2400-pmic-gpio"), as the D2089's, instead of a separate
 "apple,pmic-events" binding and "-pmic-events" compatibles; the D2400 GPIO
 inputs added for the Smart Cover hall sensors.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml  | 20 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
index d8273ae9f..8b1a3d0c0 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
@@ -19,6 +19,11 @@ description: |
   currently supported; direction switching and PMU event interrupts are not.
   Boards must reserve lines that must remain under firmware control.
 
+  The August D2400 used with the Apple A10X has 16 GPIOs whose input
+  levels are read as on the D2365; its line configuration is not known, so
+  they are inputs as the boot firmware set them up. It latches 256 PMU
+  events, GPIO line N being event 0x30 + N.
+
   The D2207 and D2365 also latch 112 and 240 PMU events respectively
   (charger, ADC, GPIO edges and others) in one read-to-clear block and
   signal them on a single active-low line to the AP. As an interrupt
@@ -30,8 +35,9 @@ description: |
   edge flags are accepted.
 
   The Dialog D2089 PMIC used with the Apple A7 latches the same 112 events
-  in the same block as the D2207. Only that event controller is described:
-  its GPIO lines and the events they raise are not, so the node is no GPIO
+  in the same block as the D2207, and the D2355 charger PMU used with the
+  Apple A10X latches 80. Only those event controllers are described: their
+  GPIO lines and the events they raise are not, so the node is no GPIO
   controller.
 
   Interrupt 112 (D2089, D2207) or 240 (D2365), one past the last event, is
@@ -47,7 +53,9 @@ properties:
       - apple,d2186-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2207-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2333-pmic-gpio
+      - apple,d2355-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2365-pmic-gpio
+      - apple,d2400-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2401-pmic-gpio
 
   gpio-controller: true
@@ -95,7 +103,9 @@ allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
-          const: apple,d2089-pmic-gpio
+          enum:
+            - apple,d2089-pmic-gpio
+            - apple,d2355-pmic-gpio
     then:
       properties:
         gpio-controller: false
@@ -135,7 +145,9 @@ allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
-          const: apple,d2365-pmic-gpio
+          enum:
+            - apple,d2365-pmic-gpio
+            - apple,d2400-pmic-gpio
     then:
       properties:
         apple,wake-events:
